      "category": "lexical",
      "criterion": "ambiguous_shall",
      "justification": "“shall” can state an obligation, a discretion, a recommendation or a prediction, and the sentence does not say which. The Federal Plain Language Guidelines (2011, p. 25) recommend “must” for an obligation, “may” for a discretionary action and “should” for a recommendation; “will” for a prediction is Lucid's note. Lucid does not pick the reading and does not replace the word: only the author knows what is meant.",
